le of Napoleon in a Robot Chicken  sketch and recorded a number of  commercials of Pedro himself ef'n  Ramirez to promote the 2005 Utah State  Fair you see flipping sasquatches around  here Plus in 2014  heeda played the part of napoleon  bonaparte Steen aged Mutant Ninja  Turtles this is to say nothing of the  many interviews in which in the middle  of promoting something entirely  different he's asked to reform a famous  line he  polian did you wet the bed last night  hey dawn did you take a dump in your bed  last night that uh that was perfect  happily Heda takes it all in stride and  he's never lost any gratitude for his  iconic role in 2018 he told The Herald  Tribune parents are introducing it to  their kids friends are introducing it to  their younger friends 14 years since it  came out I think it will always relate  to youth culture and the awkwardness of  being young and being on your own  without any responsibility in the years  since the Poli and dynamite Peter has  been presented with plenty of  opportunities he keeps the details to  himself for the most part but it's clear  that he's turned down more than a few  chances to be part of some projects that  ended up going the distance while some  might see this as foolish heeda  considers it an asset because of his  early work he can pick and choose  exactly what kind of work he wants to do  and figure out a work-life balance few  actors get to have in 2012 he told  vulture I realized how happy I am trying  to be somewhat normal without becoming  huge and not so much normal but grounded  down-to-earth he also compared his work  to that of his father a family doctor  the two professions may appear quite  different but he does always wanted the  same level of community and quiets in  his life this allows him the option of  saying no to projects he finds  distasteful like raunchy comedies though  he's not strayed too far from his comedy  roots Heder does dip a toe into the  world of dramatic film now and then 